      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article presents a case where directional coronary atherectomy was successfully performed on an occluded left main coronary artery in a cardiogenic shock patient in an emergency setting where thrombolytic agents were contraindicated. Further investigation is suggested and warranted and use of DCA may aid in management of cardiogenic shock patients."},
